  "decision_conditions": [
    "Reason : 1 - The proposed cycle and bin store by virtue of its size, design and appearance would appear incongruous and would result in the loss of the existing attractive characteristic front boundary wall feature in this location and therefore would fail to respect the character and appearance of the existing front boundary of the host building and adjoining terrace of properties. As such, the development is considered contrary to the requirements of Policy D1 (Design) of the Camden Local Plan 2017 and Policy 2 (Design and Character) of the Fortune Green and West Hampstead Neighbourhood Plan 2015.",
    "Reason : 2 - The proposed cycle and bin store by virtue of its integral doors which would open onto the public footway would have a detrimental impact on pedestrian movements and public safety. As such, the development is considered contrary to the requirements of Policy T1 (Prioritising walking, cycling and public transport) of the Camden Local Plan 2017, the Council's Transport CPG 2021 and Policy 9 (Pavements & Pedestrians) of the Fortune Green and West Hampstead Neighbourhood Plan 2015."
